{"title":"2014 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 19","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_SpreadTheMathLove\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by SpreadTheMathLove</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There are exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> distinct rational numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/9/0c937d816a76e636ba346d281a645bca9bf6a889.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|k|&lt;200$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"71\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/3/2a3083567ef6e4c63ddf113aad1c6efad4e79b71.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[5x^2+kx+12=0\\]\" width=\"142\" height=\"16\" /> has at least one integer solution for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />.  What is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/4/bf4b9f54b97eb84c5fac5810779b2ac92a3016fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }6\\qquad \\textbf{(B) }12\\qquad \\textbf{(C) }24\\qquad \\textbf{(D) }48\\qquad \\textbf{(E) }78\\qquad$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"389\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Factor the quadratic into\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/5/fe5199e9f960b0c62e2ab49965e0ff96a0bd31f6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left(5x + \\frac{12}{n}\\right)\\left(x + n\\right) = 0\\]\" width=\"180\" height=\"43\" />\nwhere <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee5df0d5b6736df591c2c12ce45cf2d71bba5e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-n$\" width=\"24\" height=\"8\" /> is our integer solution. Then, \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/b/3eb94d8ebb2ae4384f3d40a12c2ae537ea961970.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[k = \\frac{12}{n} + 5n,\\]\" width=\"101\" height=\"37\" />\nwhich takes rational values between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/8/59820a53cf7b362f73593e85ba993fbd3aba6299.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-200$\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/3/8f37626d49b4082c9102bf930bca51277ff2eb43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$200$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/3/073998353c836f3f6e67dfb4eea9588e8800e06f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|n| \\leq 39$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"63\" height=\"18\" />, excluding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/6/2d6fc266463b33c8b1c079a50909f3fd03ed5ffd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 0$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />. This leads to an answer of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/7/7e77fe86c92a5d2fef69e7728acfcbad80c362d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\cdot 39 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(E) } 78}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"128\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Solve for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/f/acf467a467306991cbf257dce1a9d3696123e1a7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[k=-\\frac{12}{x}-5x.\\]\" width=\"115\" height=\"37\" />  Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> can be any integer in the range <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/8/0d8a6d739d6ebf4e90398304c7d024a68032a5f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[-39,0)\\cup(0,39]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"127\" height=\"18\" />  so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is rational with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/c/85cfc0c2d5ce791db5a0dc62fa47c632d10e390d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lvert k\\rvert&lt;200$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"71\" height=\"18\" />.  Hence, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/b/9ebb33edd6586e83da90f55d23ad5ffe13f4cbd7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$39+39=\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) } 78}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"149\" height=\"28\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Plug in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/7/8b7e8e0360f76071d30522d4979d1c01cb248a5d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=200$\" width=\"61\" height=\"12\" /> to find the upper limit. You will find the limit to be a number from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/3/6c3c23a5ac00d0d32f28b3a6cf221965cef9cf04.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0&lt;x&lt;-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"90\" height=\"13\" /> and one that is just below <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a4e50a9cc464b64c9142990a65a36b20ff99856.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-39.$\" width=\"35\" height=\"12\" /> All the integer values from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/e/bae5aba07d37ff6ff813107e76260fb31ad5794e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/7/08763313a15808aa4aec73b1e951c486688c2627.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-39$\" width=\"31\" height=\"12\" /> can be attainable through some value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />. Since the question asks for the absolute value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />, we see that the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/2/542b0ae22b1a061c15623a86cebfd1a6190c6208.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$39\\cdot2 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(E)  }78.}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"135\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>iron\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_SpreadTheMathLove\">Video Solution by SpreadTheMathLove</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by SpreadTheMathLove\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BoPnuYKBq30\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BoPnuYKBq30</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A\" title=\"2014 AMC 12A\">2014 AMC 12A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2014 AMC 12A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2014 AMC 12A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2014 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 18\">Problem 18</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2014 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 20\">Problem 20</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_1\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2014 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2014 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_3\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2014 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_4\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2014 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_5\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2014 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/ind